<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day Treasury bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day Treasury bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 9.865 percent on Wednesday from 9.946 percent at the previous auction on March 12.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt had asked for 700 million stg and accepted bids for 761.75 million, rejecting bids for 881.75 million. Bills worth 768.525 million mature on Thursday.</p>
<p>The central bank announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: June 19, 1997 (June 12, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.865 percent (9.946)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 761.750 million (872.950 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,643.500 million (982.950 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.699-9.880 percent (8.390-10.074)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.699-10.048 percent (8.390-10.099)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 40 (154)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 159 (157)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
